From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2025 11:03:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Make ispif_reset go though VFE user
 counting logic

VFE users are counted on calls to vfe_get/put such that VFE remains
enabled as long as it has a single user. ispif_reset overrides this
and directly enables/disables VFE power domains and clocks through
different functions, meaning if there are existing VFE users when
ispif_reset is called, it will simply cut them off. Additionally,
once the last of existing users calls vfe_put, it leads to calling
device_link_del with a NULL vfe->genpd_link causing a NULL pointer
dereference.

To avoid this, make ispif_reset go through the same counting logic
as regular consumers. Since resetting ISPIF does not need to fully
power on VFE but rather only its power domain and clocks, separate
handling those into new functions that can be called from both
ispif_reset and vfe_get/put. The ispif_reset routine also enables/
disables power domains and clocks of both VFE instances regardless
of which one the reset is issued for, so now only power on/off the
relevant resources. camss_pm_domain_on/off were only used here so
remove them, as well as clock_for_reset in platform resource structs.

Signed-off-by: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
